A copy of the License is in internal/themes/LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt. The
source repository has no NOTICE file. PlantUML modified these files (it
replaced their comment header with a YAML metadata header); this project
ships them as PlantUML v1.2026.8 does.

The following upstream themes are not bundled:

- sunlust (Artem V. Ageev): its header declares the license "GPL 3+"
  (GPL-3.0-or-later), which cannot be distributed under this project's MIT
  License.
- _none_ (The-Lum), amiga, blueprint, crt-amber, crt-green, mimeograph,
  plain (Matthew Leather), mono (Denis Bondarenko and Matthew Leather) and
  carbon-gray (Bharat Rajagopalan): their files have no license line, and
  neither the upstream history of the files (the commits and pull requests
  that added them) nor upstream's LICENSES.md states a license for them, so
  their license could not be verified.

For these names, "!theme <name>" reports upstream's error for an unknown
theme ("Cannot load theme <name>"), unless a local file
puml-theme-<name>.puml is found, and %get_all_theme() does not list them.

Attributions for other assets are added here when they are bundled.
